# Information Disclosure - Framework Version Disclosure via Unhandled Exception

## Executive Summary

An information disclosure vulnerability was identified in the product retrieval functionality of the application. The `productId` parameter is not properly validated before being processed, allowing an attacker to trigger an unhandled exception by supplying an unexpected data type.

Instead of returning a generic error page, the application exposes a full Java stack trace, revealing internal implementation details, including the exact version of the web framework in use: **Apache Struts 2 2.3.31**.

Although this issue does not directly compromise confidentiality, integrity, or availability, it significantly aids attackers during the reconnaissance phase by exposing valuable information that can be used to identify publicly known vulnerabilities affecting the disclosed framework version.

