---

# Key Takeaways

* Verbose error messages should never be exposed in production environments.
* Stack traces provide attackers with valuable reconnaissance information.
* Framework version disclosure can significantly simplify vulnerability research.
* Proper input validation and centralized exception handling reduce unnecessary information leakage.
* Production systems should return generic error responses while logging detailed exceptions internally.
